<title>BELGIUM: Belgian money market supply raised in week.</title>
<headline>Belgian money market supply raised in week.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian central bank said it added liquidity to the money market in the week to February 17 to offset a rise in notes in circulation and sight deposits.</p>
<p>(figures from the weekly statement in bln francs) -</p>
<p> Foreign currency reserves	   181.71 (+    1.19)</p>
<p> Advances against pledged security  13.45 (+    0.29)</p>
<p> Commercial bills			  2.82 (+    0.08)</p>
<p> Securities portfolio		   24.83 (+    0.00)</p>
<p> Money market interventions*	  90.49 (+    2.07)</p>
<p> Bank notes in circulation	   447.04 (+    0.96)</p>
<p>* comprises repurchase agreements and interbank loans</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
